.Dd June 14, 2026
.Dt MBT_HEX 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mbt_hex_decode ,
.Nm mbt_hex_encode
.Nd Hexadecimal encoding and decoding
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/hex.h
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_hex_decode "unsigned char *buf" "size_t len" "const char *str"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_hex_encode "unsigned char *buf" "size_t blen" "char *str" "size_t slen"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn mbt_hex_decode
decodes a hexadecimal string into a byte buffer.
The
.Fa str
parameter is the input hexadecimal string.
The
.Fa buf
parameter is the destination buffer, and
.Fa len
is the size of that buffer in bytes.
Returns 0 on success, or a negative error code on failure (e.g., if the string contains non-hex characters or is too long for the buffer).
.Pp
.Fn mbt_hex_encode
encodes a byte buffer into a hexadecimal string.
The
.Fa buf
parameter is the source byte buffer, and
.Fa blen
is its length in bytes.
The
.Fa str
parameter is the destination buffer for the resulting hex string, and
.Fa slen
is the size of that buffer in bytes.
Returns 0 on success, or a negative error code on failure (e.g., if there's not enough space in the destination buffer).
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Functions returning
.Ft int
return 0 on success or a negative errno value on failure.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Decoding and encoding hex:
.Bd -literal
unsigned char decoded[4];
const char *hex = "41424344";

if (mbt_hex_decode(decoded, 4, hex) == 0) {
    // decoded now contains {'A', 'B', 'C', 'D'}
}

char encoded[9]; // 8 chars + null terminator
if (mbt_hex_encode(decoded, 4, encoded, sizeof(encoded)) == 0) {
    // encoded now contains "41424344"
}
.Ed
